  "content": {
    "id": "p26-q33-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "33",
    "prompt": "A bag contains $n$ numbers from 1 through to $n$. One number is chosen from the bag. The number is returned, and then a second number is chosen.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p26-q33-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the probability that both numbers are the same.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{1}{n}$",
          "worked": "There are $n^2$ equally likely ordered pairs. The $n$ pairs $(1,1),(2,2),\\ldots,(n,n)$ have equal numbers.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{same})&=\\frac{n}{n^2}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{same})&=\\frac{1}{n}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q33-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, find the probability that the first number exceeds the second.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{n-1}{2n}$\n\nThe unequal outcomes split equally between the first number being larger and the second number being larger.",
          "worked": "Interchanging the two numbers pairs every outcome with the first number larger with an equally likely outcome with the second number larger. Hence each event has half the probability of unequal numbers.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{first exceeds second})&=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\frac{1}{n}\\right)\\\\\\Pr(\\text{first exceeds second})&=\\frac{n-1}{2n}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      }
    ]
  },
